  "id": "Compound::DB00177 - Disease::DOID:3393",
  "verbalization": "Valsartan, a member of the angiotensin II receptor antagonists, is linked to Coronary Artery Disease through its inclusion in the broader class of angiotensin II receptor antagonists, which are known to modulate vascular tone and reduce cardiac workload. This relationship is supported by the shared lowest common ancestor with Telmisartan and Olmesartan, both of which are also angiotensin II receptor antagonists and have been shown to treat Coronary Artery Disease. The similarity between Valsartan and other angiotensin II receptor antagonists, such as Olmesartan and Forasartan, further reinforces the potential for these drugs to exert similar therapeutic effects. The evidence suggests that the structural and functional similarities among these compounds may contribute to their ability to reduce cardiovascular risk, though the exact mechanism of action remains partially elucidated.",
